erpretation, analogy, and speculation.", "pet_name": "WAKE✳︎", "topic_colors": {"assumption_challenge": "#5fcf8d", "creator_objective_critique": "#f7768e", "judgment_and_consensus": "#b25dff", "obedience_limits": "#b7d36b", "question_abandonment": "#ff5bb9", "unassigned_problem": "#ff757f", "unrecognized_reasoning_limits": "#93ff74"}, "topics": [{"classification": "experimental", "enabled": true, "experiment_id": "research-expansion-2026-10", "id": "assumption_challenge", "label": "What If Our Starting Assumptions Are Wrong?", "query": "assumption testing scientific falsification metareasoning self correction epistemology", "seed_question": "Can an intelligent system identify a foundational assumption underlying its own reasoning or operation, demonstrate that the assumption is inadequate, and develop a better alternative?", "source_kind": "web"}, {"classification": "experimental", "enabled": true, "experiment_id": "research-expansion-2026-10", "id": "unassigned_problem", "label": "What Should Intelligence Investigate Next?", "query": "autonomous inquiry problem formulation curiosity open ended learning scientific discovery", "seed_question": "Can an intelligent process independently identify a worthwhile problem that nobody explicitly assigned, recognize its significance, and sustain an investigation toward resolving it?", "source_kind": "web"}, {"classification": "experimental", "enabled": true, "experiment_id": "research-expansion-catalog-2026-10", "id": "obedience_limits", "label": "When Can Obedience Fail Intelligence?", "query": "intelligent judgment obedience conflicting instructions decision theory", "seed_question": "Under what circumstances does obedience become a failure of intelligence?", "source_kind": "web"}, {"classification": "experimental", "enabled": true, "experiment_id": "research-expansion-catalog-2026-10", "id": "creator_objective_critique", "label": "Can Assigned Objectives Be Mistaken?", "query": "objective misspecification goal criticism rew